-- =============================================================================
--  server/src/models/sql/tables.sql
-- =============================================================================
--  Canonical CREATE TABLE definitions for every table in the source schema.
--  This file is regenerated by `scripts/dump-source-schema.ts` from the live
--  Supabase database, so it is guaranteed to match production byte-for-byte.
--
--  IMPORTANT — Auth boundary rewrite:
--    The source schema has a handful of FKs pointing at `auth.users(id)` (a
--    Supabase-managed table that does not exist on Railway). The dumper
--    rewrites those FKs to reference `public.profiles(id) ON DELETE SET NULL`
--    instead, because `profiles.id` is 1:1 with the user id in every existing
--    row. This preserves referential integrity without depending on Supabase
--    Auth. The affected column today is:
--        challenge_milestones.coords_updated_by → profiles(id) ON DELETE SET NULL
--
--  DO NOT hand-edit — run:
--      npm run schema:dump   (writes tables.sql, indexes.sql, functions.sql,
--                             triggers.sql, grants.sql, rollback.sql)
--
--  When this file is empty, the migration is a no-op — used only for local
--  scaffolding before the dump has been produced. `scripts/validate-schema.ts`
--  enforces that all 28 expected tables exist post-migrate.
-- =============================================================================
